Yes — your test suite is now basically fixed. 19 tests ran and only 1 failed, and the failure is purely because of an unnecessary Mockito stub.

The failing test is:

sendFlexRequest - non shipment endpoint does not use performance URL

The problem is at line 868, where the test is probably doing something like:

when(perfTestDeterminer.usePerfTestUrl()).thenReturn(true);

But for a non-shipment endpoint, usePerfTestUrl() is never called, so Mockito reports the stub as unnecessary.

Replace only this test

Use this version:

@Test
void sendFlexRequest_nonShipmentEndpoint_doesNotUsePerformanceUrl() throws Exception {

    String endpoint = "some-other-endpoint";

    server.enqueue(
        new MockResponse()
            .setResponseCode(200)
            .setHeader("Content-Type", "application/json")
            .setBody("{}"));

    // No stubbing of perfTestDeterminer is required here.
    // Non-shipment endpoints do not call usePerfTestUrl().
    subject
        .sendFlexRequest(
            endpoint,
            HttpMethod.POST,
            Map.of(),
            new Object(),
            Object.class)
        .block();

    RecordedRequest recordedRequest =
        server.takeRequest(2, TimeUnit.SECONDS);

    assertNotNull(recordedRequest);

    assertEquals(
        "/some-other-endpoint",
        recordedRequest.getPath());

    assertEquals(
        "POST",
        recordedRequest.getMethod());
}

